  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $S$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SP}=\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/07aebf5a6aaa98c9ec5d4e9801dbe7d2cf3ade86573bcd8ee56db375f3e38575.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{ST}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{TQ}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QP}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/7c8c193472acbe72979f8a78fe9bd02726ad98c166381434175d0586bb574cb6.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SP} & =\\overset{\\to }{ST}+\\overset{\\to }{TQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP} \\\\  & =a+b+d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
